<%# THE CUT LINE — where the prize money stops. Locals: contest, collapsed.

    Mid-contest a leaderboard is a list of numbers going up, and the one fact it
    never states is the only one that decides whether a score matters: is this
    entry still being paid? The per-row prize labels answer it for the rows that
    ARE paid and say nothing at all about the row directly beneath them, which is
    the row whose owner most needs to know.

    Drawn once, between the last paying rank and the first that pays nothing, so
    the two sides of it read as different places to be.

    `collapsed` mirrors the row above it into the collapsed tail: on a format that
    pays nine (large), the cut falls below the eight-row fold, and a divider that
    stayed visible while its neighbours were hidden would point at nothing. %>
<div <% if collapsed %>x-show="expanded" x-cloak <% end %>class="flex items-center gap-3 px-1 py-1"
     data-test="leaderboard-money-line" role="separator"
     aria-label="Below this line, entries are out of the money">
  <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-primary/60"></span>
  <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap">
    <%= dollars(contest.payouts.values.sum / 100.0) %> paid above
  </span>
  <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-l from-transparent to-primary/60"></span>
</div>
